{"schema_version":1,"task_id":"code-6261fff562f42807","paper_id":"2208.04654v1","variant":"original","kind":"code","outcome":"checked","reason":null,"error":null,"findings":[{"finding_id":"code-6261fff562f42807-f0","task_id":"code-6261fff562f42807","paper_id":"2208.04654v1","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"summary":"The paper states that LeakyReLU activations are used in each layer in both networks, but the fourth layer of the feature extraction network f_theta is configured with a 'linear' activation rather than 'leaky_relu'.","explanation":"Model discrepancy, high confidence.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2208.04654v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"In both networks, we use BatchNorm [18] and LeakyReLU [19] activations in each layer.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc@2210bf55395669c1c39d49f65f286fc9a1523fc9","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc"},"text":"                          'cnn_N_filt': [128, 128, 128, num_channels],\n                          'cnn_len_filt': [1023, 11, 9, 7],\n                          'cnn_max_pool_len': [1, 1, 1, 1],\n                          'cnn_use_laynorm_inp': False,\n                          'cnn_use_batchnorm_inp': False,\n                          'cnn_use_laynorm': [False, False, False, False],\n                          'cnn_use_batchnorm': [True, True, True, True],\n                          'cnn_act': ['leaky_relu', 'leaky_relu', 'leaky_relu', 'linear'],\n                          'cnn_drop': [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0],","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"model.py","line_start":102,"line_end":110}],"uncertain":false},{"finding_id":"code-6261fff562f42807-f1","task_id":"code-6261fff562f42807","paper_id":"2208.04654v1","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"summary":"The model g_theta outputs unnormalized logits directly from final_conv without applying softmax normalization in the final layer.","explanation":"Model discrepancy, high confidence.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2208.04654v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"In order to output a probability distribution over time shifts, the GCC-PHAT output is fed into another network g θ : R (2τmax+1)×L → R (2τmax+1) , with its own set of parameters θ that combines the L different correlations and applies softmax normalization in the final layer.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc@2210bf55395669c1c39d49f65f286fc9a1523fc9","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc"},"text":"        s = cc.shape[2]\n        padding = get_pad(\n            size=s, kernel_size=self.final_kernel, stride=1, dilation=1)\n        cc = F.pad(cc, pad=padding, mode='constant')\n        cc = self.final_conv(cc).reshape([batch_size, -1])\n        if self.head == 'regression':\n            cc = self.reg(cc).squeeze()\n\n        return cc","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"model.py","line_start":151,"line_end":159}],"uncertain":false},{"finding_id":"code-6261fff562f42807-f2","task_id":"code-6261fff562f42807","paper_id":"2208.04654v1","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"summary":"The evaluation configuration in the code sets t60_range to [0.2, 0.4, 0.6], omitting 0.8 s and 1.0 s from the evaluation grid.","explanation":"Evaluation discrepancy, high confidence.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2208.04654v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"Each recording was evaluated for SNRs ∈ {0, 6, 12, 18, 24, 30} dB and reverberation times T60 ∈ {0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8, 1} s.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc@2210bf55395669c1c39d49f65f286fc9a1523fc9","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc"},"text":"snr_range = [0, 6, 12, 18, 24, 30]\nt60_range = [0.2, 0.4, 0.6]","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"cfg.py","line_start":27,"line_end":28}],"uncertain":false}],"attempts":1}
